[2026-09-30 10:47-10:54]
Attempted the complete Base command with the teacher-recommended Java 8 RI:
java -jar SPECjvm2008.jar --base

The run passed kit validation and the functional check, then hung in startup.compiler.sunflow. A thread dump showed the benchmark thread blocked in FileOutputStream.writeBytes while javac emitted diagnostics. SPEC's official FAQ and Known Issues state that these four compiler workloads do not run on Java SE 8 or later:
- startup.compiler.compiler
- startup.compiler.sunflow
- compiler.compiler
- compiler.sunflow

Excluding them would not satisfy the requested complete Base run, and modifying the benchmark would invalidate its checksum. The hung process was therefore stopped without claiming a result. Evidence:
- logs/base_run_java8_failed.log
- logs/startup_sunflow_hang_jstack.txt

